insert into public.moo_versions (id,document_id,label,body_md,change_note,status) values
('727c8f79-41fe-5581-beb8-108a7e526cdb'::uuid,'4744143d-bf31-58ae-a850-aa662ce66fd7'::uuid,'v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7)',E'# Annex 5-C. Pre-disaster Recovery Framework Outline\n\n1.  Purpose, scope and adoption (CDRRMC resolution, version, review date).\n\n2.  Recovery principles: Build Back Better, inclusion, local ownership, privacy.\n\n3.  Recovery baseline summary by barangay (Annex 5-E) and known data gaps.\n\n4.  Recovery scenarios per priority hazard (most probable and most severe) and the recovery needs they imply.\n\n5.  Critical areas, assets and population groups, in order of recovery priority.\n\n6.  Recovery organisation: Rehabilitation and Recovery Committee, sub-committees, lead offices and focal persons.\n\n7.  PDNA activation: triggers, decision route, team designations, templates and OCD VIII support arrangements.\n\n8.  Temporary shelter and evacuation centre closure arrangements (with CSWDO and the housing office).\n\n9.  Debris and post-disaster waste management (with ENRO and City Engineering).\n\n10. Scalable and reprogrammable PPAs by office.\n\n11. Recovery financing map: fund sources, insurance status of City assets, farmer enrolment, partner commitments.\n\n12. Pre-agreed partnership arrangements (MOAs with private sector, CSOs, academe and suppliers; Chapter 8).\n\n13. Monitoring unit, matrix and reporting arrangements.\n\n14. Communication strategy template and feedback channels.\n\n15. Annual review record and lessons from recent events.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch5v1_Annex_5-C.md (Chapter 5, v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7))','draft'),
('f3f1a168-1048-5e58-801a-0d61581a8f54'::uuid,'331670a4-51ad-58d6-b959-6e99b51b8d48'::uuid,'v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7)',E'# Annex 5-D. Recovery Monitoring Matrix Fields (REC-F06)\n\n**Table 5.42**\n\n*Minimum Fields of the Recovery Monitoring Matrix*\n\n| **Field group**    | **Fields**                                                                                           | **Source**               |\n|--------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|--------------------------|\n| **Identification** | Event; PPA ID; title; sector; sub-committee; phase (early recovery, short term, medium term)         | REC-F04                  |\n| **Location**       | PSGC barangay code(s); site description (no personal data)                                           | REC-F04                  |\n| **Link to need**   | PDNA reference; ER-F05 line (if from transition); BBB screen reference                               | PDNA; REC-F02; REC-F07   |\n| **Targets**        | Output indicator; target by year; unit; beneficiaries as aggregates by sex, age group and disability | Program                  |\n| **Finance**        | Approved cost; fund source; obligations; disbursements                                               | Chapter 6 records        |\n| **Implementation** | Implementing office; partner; start and planned completion; percentage physical accomplishment       | Office reports           |\n| **Issues**         | Issue; owner; decision; due date                                                                     | Problem-solving meetings |\n| **Verification**   | Field validation date; BBB conditions met (yes/no); evidence link                                    | SOP 5-05, 5-07           |\n| **Closeout**       | Completion date; closeout evidence; outcome note; lesson reference (Chapter 7)                       | REC-F09                  |\n\n*Note.* Blank means "not reported", never zero. Figures are scoped to one event. The matrix is the event-database extension recommended for A9.3 and links to the A5.4 event database of Chapter 3.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch5v1_Annex_5-D.md (Chapter 5, v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7))','draft'),
('5b6bdb86-42c2-5d85-9c1e-eeedc554b7f4'::uuid,'497fd21a-3aee-5932-9466-f989cdd0d8b6'::uuid,'v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7)',E'# Annex 5-E. Minimum Data for the Recovery Baseline\n\n**Table 5.43**\n\n*Minimum Recovery Baseline Data, Disaggregation and Source*\n\n| **Element**                          | **Data and disaggregation**                                                                        | **Likely source**                  |\n|--------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|------------------------------------|\n| **General information**              | Land area; topography; barangay boundaries (PSGC)                                                  | CPDO; CLUP; NAMRIA; PSA            |\n| **Income and poverty**               | Income class; poverty incidence by barangay                                                        | BLGF; PSA; CBMS                    |\n| **Population**                       | Total population by barangay, urban/rural, sex, age group and disability                           | PSA; CBMS                          |\n| **Settlements and housing**          | Settlement areas and population; housing materials; informal settlers; land use and zoning map     | CLUP; Shelter Plan; CDRA           |\n| **Economic activity and livelihood** | Labour force; MSMEs; farmers and fisherfolk; agricultural areas and facilities; informal sector    | PESO; BPLO; City Agriculture; CDRA |\n| **Infrastructure and lifelines**     | Roads and bridges; power, water and telecom facilities; port; public buildings; evacuation centres | City Engineering; utilities; CDRA  |\n| **Social services**                  | Schools; health facilities; social welfare facilities and caseloads (aggregates)                   | DepEd; CHO; CSWDO                  |\n| **Environment**                      | Protected areas; watersheds; forest and mangrove cover                                             | CENRO; DENR; LCCAP                 |\n| **Hazards and past events**          | Hazard maps; past damage and losses by event                                                       | CDRA; RDANA and PDNA reports       |\n\n*Note.* Adapted from Annex A of the NEDA (2020) guide. Household-level data stays with the source office; the baseline holds aggregates by barangay.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch5v1_Annex_5-E.md (Chapter 5, v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7))','draft'),
('8d0e05eb-d7dd-594c-9845-ba0e2c256116'::uuid,'dc1c4086-d8bb-592d-b44e-2cbe3f900597'::uuid,'v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7)',E'# Annex 7-A. IAT and Master Requirements Traceability\n\n**Table 7.39**\n\n*IAT Rows, Master Requirements and Chapter 7 Procedures*\n\n| **IAT** | **Type** | **w** | **Score** | **Gap priority** | **Master requirements**              | **SOP**           | **Recommended action (IAT v1.7)**                                                                                                                           |\n|---------|----------|-------|-----------|------------------|--------------------------------------|-------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| A10.3   | M        | 2     | 3         | 3.0 Low          | MR-02; MR-07; MR-01; MR-12–15        | Section 10        | Adopt RDRRMC VIII Res. No. 12-006 locally by CDRRMC resolution; confirm the harmonized template is used.                                                    |\n| A10.4   | M        | 2     | 2         | 6.0 Medium       | MR-07; MR-11; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 7-01              | Produce the first annual RBME report (Form 5D) and baseline database; present it to the CDRRMC and LDC; include IAT results and CDRA monitoring indicators. |\n| A10.6   | GP       | 2     | 2         | 4.0 Medium       | MR-07; MR-11; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 7-04, 7-05        | Validate AAR reports and the plan revisions they produced.                                                                                                  |\n| A10.8   | M        | 2     | 0         | 12.0 High        | MR-07; MR-11; MR-16; MR-01; MR-12–15 | 7-06              | Prepare the 45-day post-declaration report template and confirm the route with OCD VIII.                                                                    |\n| A10.9   | GP       | 1     | 2         | 2.0 Low          | MR-11; MR-18; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 7-08              | Document changes adopted from exchanges.                                                                                                                    |\n| A5.4    | GP       | 2     | 0         | 8.0 Medium       | MR-03; MR-07; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 7-07              | Set up a disaster event and loss database (Sendai and DesInventar fields) and back-load past RDANA and PDNA data.                                           |\n| A5.5    | M        | 2     | 2         | 6.0 Medium       | MR-03; MR-07; MR-10; MR-01; MR-12–15 | 7-09              | Confirm the City DPO; sign data-sharing agreements with CSWDO and CPDO; add privacy notices to registration forms.                                          |\n| B7.3    | M        | 2     | 2         | 6.0 Medium       | MR-04; MR-11; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 7-04 (evaluation) | Run an annual exercise program testing EOC activation (Chapter 9); evaluate each exercise here.                                                             |\n| B7.4    | GP       | 2     | 2         | 4.0 Medium       | MR-04; MR-11; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 7-04, 7-05        | Track AAR actions in an improvement plan.                                                                                                                   |\n\n*Note.* Copied from IAT v1.7 and the Traceability and Data Dictionary v1.2. Scores and priorities are for validation (Methodology v1.1, section 6). SOPs 7-02 and 7-03 serve all 140 indicators and MR-12 to MR-15.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch7v1_Annex_7-A.md (Chapter 7, v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7))','draft'),
('7dee14ee-e033-5481-828f-90f394167242'::uuid,'7d4d0440-bc6c-5e93-94dc-62c804432e55'::uuid,'v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7)',E'# Annex 7-B. LDRRMP M&E Matrix Template\n\nOne row per indicator. Aligned with Form 5D of the Ormoc City DRRM 10-Year Plan and the M&E matrix of the NDRRMP 2020–2030 RBME Plan.\n\n**Table 7.40**\n\n*M&E Matrix Columns (ME-F01)*\n\n| **Column**                   | **Content**                                                               |\n|------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| **Code and result level**    | Unique code; impact, outcome, output or input and process                 |\n| **Indicator and definition** | What is counted, how, and what is excluded                                |\n| **Unit and disaggregation**  | Unit; sex, age, disability and barangay where relevant                    |\n| **Baseline**                 | Value and year, with source                                               |\n| **Targets**                  | By year to 2032, as approved by the CDRRMC                                |\n| **Data source and method**   | Office records, surveys, SitReps, IAT, database                           |\n| **Frequency**                | Quarterly, annual or per event                                            |\n| **Responsible office**       | Thematic focal office and data provider                                   |\n| **Framework codes**          | Ten Essentials; NDRRMP outcome; DILG pillar; Sendai target; IAT indicator |\n| **Current value and status** | Value, date, on-track or off-track, explanation                           |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch7v1_Annex_7-B.md (Chapter 7, v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7))','draft'),
('00921f31-3f01-5734-9b24-70939b0dcd5b'::uuid,'b81dbeb4-0ca3-5539-ad44-fbd6fe409922'::uuid,'v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7)',E'# Annex 7-C. After-Action Review Report Outline\n\n**Table 7.41**\n\n*Contents of an AAR Report (ME-F03)*\n\n| **No.** | **Section**                 | **Content**                                                                                |\n|---------|-----------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| 1       | Event and scope             | Event or exercise, dates, hazard, area, EOC level, declarations; what the AAR covers       |\n| 2       | Method and participants     | Facilitator; offices and positions taking part; sources used                               |\n| 3       | Timeline                    | Official warning products with IDs; decisions; activations; key SitReps; resource requests |\n| 4       | What was supposed to happen | Plans, SOPs and protocols that applied                                                     |\n| 5       | What happened               | Facts, with evidence                                                                       |\n| 6       | What worked                 | Practices to keep, with evidence                                                           |\n| 7       | What did not work and why   | Findings with root or contributing causes; single- or double-loop                          |\n| 8       | Actions                     | Recommended actions with owner, due date and resources, entered in the CAPA register       |\n| 9       | Inclusion and protection    | How women, children, older persons and persons with disabilities were reached; gaps        |\n| 10      | Approval                    | CDRRMO Head approval; items referred to the CDRRMC                                         |\n\n*Note.* Records name positions, not individuals. Personal data of affected people is not included.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch7v1_Annex_7-C.md (Chapter 7, v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7))','draft'),
('4b4ea8e9-bbbd-550e-a440-3abb3df8c91d'::uuid,'e61be13d-6512-5352-9b3b-5b8178fee3cc'::uuid,'v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7)',E'# Annex 7-D. Post-Declaration (45-day) Report Outline\n\nBasis: RA 12287 IRR Rule VI Sec. 1. The required content (declaration status, AA fund utilisation, estimated economic and social costs minimised) is followed; the remaining sections are proposed to make the report usable for learning. The outline will be revised when the NDRRMC issues the AA monitoring and evaluation framework.\n\n**Table 7.42**\n\n*Contents of the 45-day Report*\n\n| **No.** | **Section**                         | **Content**                                                                                                                     | **Basis**                     |\n|---------|-------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------|\n| 1       | Declaration status                  | Hazard; area; PDRA; CDRRMC recommendation; RDRRMC VIII action; Mayor''s EO; dates of declaration and lifting; ground for lifting | Rule VI Sec. 1                |\n| 2       | Anticipatory actions                | Measures carried out by lead office and barangay; people and assets covered (aggregate)                                         | Proposed                      |\n| 3       | AA fund utilisation                 | Spending by source and measure; tranche compliance; unused funds transferred to the STF                                         | Rule VI Sec. 1; Rule V Sec. 3 |\n| 4       | Economic and social costs minimised | Estimate with method and assumptions                                                                                            | Rule VI Sec. 1                |\n| 5       | Lessons                             | Summary of the AAR findings and actions                                                                                         | Proposed                      |\n| 6       | Annexes                             | EO; lifting record (GOV-F12); FIN-F06 closure                                                                                   | Proposed                      |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch7v1_Annex_7-D.md (Chapter 7, v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7))','draft'),
('06bfc02d-7532-50d0-8821-3307aa5d772b'::uuid,'b83a91de-80b0-53ca-b792-f9e4baf07a63'::uuid,'v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7)',E'# Annex 7-E. Disaster Event and Loss Database Fields\n\n**Table 7.43**\n\n*Minimum Fields of the Event and Loss Record (ME-F07)*\n\n| **Field group**                      | **Fields**                                                                                                                                     | **Sendai link** |\n|--------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------|\n| Event                                | Event ID; name; hazard type; start and end dates; source agency product IDs; declarations in force                                             | —               |\n| Location                             | Barangays affected (PSGC codes); area description                                                                                              | —               |\n| Human effects                        | Dead; missing; injured; affected persons and families; displaced in and outside evacuation centres (aggregate, by sex and age where available) | A, B            |\n| Housing                              | Houses partially and totally damaged                                                                                                           | B, C            |\n| Economic loss                        | Direct loss by sector (agriculture, infrastructure, housing, business), PHP, with valuation method                                             | C               |\n| Critical infrastructure and services | Damaged health and education facilities, roads, bridges, power and water; duration of service disruption                                       | D               |\n| Response and AA                      | Whether an EOC activation, State of Calamity or State of Imminent Disaster applied; AA carried out                                             | G               |\n| Sources and quality                  | Source document for each figure; date; quality flag; reviewer                                                                                  | —               |\n\n*Note.* Aggregate counts only. Blank means "not reported". Small counts are reviewed by the DPO before publication.\n\n# Validation and Source Control Register\n\n**Table 7.44**\n\n*Validation and Source Control Register*\n\n| **Item**                         | **Source used**                                                      | **Status**                                                    |\n|----------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------|\n| IAT rows and scores              | IAT v1.7 workbook in the repository (12 Nov 2026)                    | Pending validation, 1–4 December 2026                         |\n| M&E design and reporting outputs | Ormoc City DRRM 10-Year Plan 2023–2032, Chapter 5 and Table 33       | Confirm Form 5D and reporting dates with the CPDO             |\n| RA 10121 Sec. 12(c) item numbers | Cited in IAT v1.7 (A5.4, A10.4)                                      | Check item numbers against the official text                  |\n| 45-day report content            | RA 12287 IRR Rule VI Sec. 1; GOV-F13                                 | Route to be confirmed with OCD VIII; AA M&E framework pending |\n| Local EOs on M&E                 | EO 2022-00020; EO 2023-0026; EO 2024-032A, as summarised in IAT v1.7 | Attach copies in the Vault                                    |\n| NPC circulars                    | NPC Circulars No. 16-03 and No. 2023-06                              | DPO to confirm current text                                   |\n| Validation controls              | ADR-029 (MODE v1.15.0)                                               | Proposed; for the CDRRMO Head to accept before the workshop   |\n| AAR and exercise timings         | Proposed by this chapter                                             | For CDRRMC adoption                                           |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch7v1_Annex_7-E.md (Chapter 7, v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7))','draft'),
('178f631a-2675-57e5-92fe-3f34a52b2418'::uuid,'19accd5e-3619-5fb2-8a61-2e9ad4691fdf'::uuid,'v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7)',E'# Annex 8-A. IAT and Master Requirements Traceability\n\n**Table 8.33**\n\n*IAT Rows, Master Requirements and Chapter 8 Procedures*\n\n| **IAT** | **Type / lead**   | **w** | **Score** | **Gap priority** | **Master requirements**              | **SOP**    | **Recommended action (IAT v1.7)**                                                                                                                |\n|---------|-------------------|-------|-----------|------------------|--------------------------------------|------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| A10.1   | GP                | 2     | 1         | 6.0 Medium       | MR-02; MR-01; MR-12–15               | 8-02, 8-08 | Reframe as technical mutual aid MOAs with Kananga, Albuera, Merida, Isabel and the Province; join the Leyte DRRMCs Telecom and Response Network. |\n| A10.2   | GP                | 1     | 3         | 1.0 Low          | MR-02; MR-18; MR-01; MR-12–15        | 8-01, 8-07 | Keep a partner register; review MOAs yearly at a CDRRMC meeting; file signed copies; add AA roles and resource commitments.                      |\n| A1.2    | M                 | 2     | 3         | 3.0 Low          | MR-02; MR-01; MR-12–15               | 8-06       | Amend EO 2024-032A: City College of Ormoc and an academe seat; third private seat; SP accreditation of each CSO.                                 |\n| A8.5    | M                 | 2     | 3         | 3.0 Low          | MR-05; MR-01; MR-12–15               | 8-03       | Adopt a cluster EO aligned to the national clusters, naming lead and member offices (Chapter 4).                                                 |\n| B6.6    | GP                | 2     | 1         | 6.0 Medium       | MR-08; MR-16; MR-18; MR-01; MR-12–15 | 8-01, 8-05 | Sign agreements listing item, quantity, trigger and contact, usable for AA (Chapter 6).                                                          |\n| C1.1    | CPDO              | 2     | 2         | 4.0 Medium       | MR-03; MR-17; MR-18                  | 8-04       | Define most-probable and most-severe scenarios; use them in CDP and CLUP priorities.                                                             |\n| C1.2    | CPDO; Budget      | 1     | 1         | 3.0 Low          | MR-03; MR-17; MR-18                  | 8-04       | Add a DRR-CCA screening form to LDC and LFC review.                                                                                              |\n| C1.3    | CPDO              | 1     | 2         | 2.0 Low          | MR-03; MR-17; MR-18                  | 8-04       | Estimate jobs, income, displacement, ecosystem and heritage losses in the CDRA update.                                                           |\n| C1.4    | CPDO; Zoning      | 2     | 2         | 4.0 Medium       | MR-03; MR-17; MR-18                  | 8-04       | Add hazard overlay zones and permit conditions in the ZO update.                                                                                 |\n| C2.1    | Bldg Official     | 3     | 1         | 9.0 High         | MR-03; MR-16; MR-17; MR-18           | 8-04, 8-05 | Assess the EOC, evacuation centres and critical facilities; write a rapid pre-impact inspection checklist.                                       |\n| C2.2    | CDRRMO; utilities | 2     | 2         | 4.0 Medium       | MR-03; MR-16; MR-17; MR-18           | 8-05       | Sign restoration-priority arrangements with power, water and telecom providers.                                                                  |\n| C2.3    | Engg; DPWH; port  | 2     | 1         | 6.0 Medium       | MR-03; MR-16; MR-17; MR-18           | 8-04       | Write transport anticipatory actions with DPWH, the City Engineer, traffic office and port.                                                      |\n| C3.1    | CENRO             | 2     | 2         | 4.0 Medium       | MR-03; MR-17; MR-18                  | 8-04       | Monitor watershed forest cover and mangroves yearly; report to the CDRRMC.                                                                       |\n| C3.2    | CENRO             | 1     | 1         | 3.0 Low          | MR-03; MR-17; MR-18                  | 8-02       | Formalise watershed arrangements with DENR, EDC and neighbouring LGUs.                                                                           |\n| C3.3    | CENRO; Engg; GSO  | 2     | 1         | 6.0 Medium       | MR-03; MR-16; MR-17                  | 8-04       | Write the declogging and debris protocol.                                                                                                        |\n| C4.1    | CHO; hospitals    | 3     | 1         | 9.0 High         | MR-05; MR-16; MR-17                  | 8-04       | Prepare the health anticipatory action plan with the CHO and hospitals.                                                                          |\n| C4.2    | DepEd SDO         | 2     | 1         | 6.0 Medium       | MR-05; MR-16; MR-17                  | 8-04       | Obtain school AA plans and learning-continuity modalities; agree class suspension and school-use triggers.                                       |\n| C4.3    | Agri; Vet         | 2     | 2         | 4.0 Medium       | MR-05; MR-16; MR-17                  | 8-04       | Draft agri-fisheries early action guidelines using RSBSA and FishR; file the El Niño Task Force plan.                                            |\n| C4.4    | DTI; market       | 1     | 1         | 3.0 Low          | MR-05; MR-16; MR-17                  | 8-04       | Agree pre-impact price monitoring with DTI Leyte and the market office.                                                                          |\n| C5.1    | CDRRMO; Chamber   | 1     | 1         | 3.0 Low          | MR-04; MR-17; MR-18                  | 8-04       | Run business continuity outreach with the Chamber using CDRA scenarios.                                                                          |\n\n*Note.* Copied from IAT v1.7 and the Traceability and Data Dictionary v1.2. For Part C rows the master requirements shown are those specific to the row; every row also carries MR-01 and MR-12 to MR-15. Part C rows carry the lead office in the Type column and are scored into the Interface Index, not the IMI.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch8v1_Annex_8-A.md (Chapter 8, v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7))','draft'),
('079453b4-df63-5dec-8017-66ca38ca18c7'::uuid,'56d898cb-21cb-5848-9051-be21ae734dc6'::uuid,'v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7)',E'# Annex 8-B. Model Outline of a Technical Mutual Aid Agreement\n\n**Table 8.34**\n\n*Outline of a Technical Mutual Aid Agreement*\n\n| **No.** | **Article**                     | **Content to be negotiated**                                                                                   |\n|---------|---------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| 1       | Parties and authority           | LGUs; sanggunian resolutions authorising each Mayor; optional accession by the Province                        |\n| 2       | Purpose and principles          | Technical cooperation in DRRM; reciprocity; no transfer of authority; each party first protects its own people |\n| 3       | Definitions                     | Requesting party, assisting party, resources, deployment, host Incident Commander                              |\n| 4       | Resources covered               | Types of teams, equipment and services; annexed lists updated yearly                                           |\n| 5       | Activation                      | Who may request; request content; response time; right to decline                                              |\n| 6       | Command, control and safety     | Under the host IC (ICS); own supervisors; right of recall                                                      |\n| 7       | Logistics                       | Self-sufficiency period; food, lodging and fuel arrangements                                                   |\n| 8       | Costs and settlement            | What each party bears; reimbursement method; timing                                                            |\n| 9       | Liability and insurance         | Personnel and equipment insurance; claims; indemnity                                                           |\n| 10      | Information and data            | Directory, warnings and SitRep exchange; data protection                                                       |\n| 11      | Exercises and review            | Annual joint exercise or call-down; annual review                                                              |\n| 12      | Term, amendment and termination | Duration; renewal; notice period                                                                               |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch8v1_Annex_8-B.md (Chapter 8, v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7))','draft'),
('03fdffa3-f1eb-552d-9ca6-2f49ede33ad2'::uuid,'8611a789-4246-5172-90b9-a283ff80c42f'::uuid,'v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7)',E'# Annex 8-C. Model Outline of a Part C Interface Agreement\n\n**Table 8.35**\n\n*Outline of an Interface Agreement Between the CDRRMO and a Lead Office*\n\n| **No.** | **Section**           | **Content**                                                                                                        |\n|---------|-----------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| 1       | Parties and approval  | CDRRMO and the lead office; approved by the City Administrator (or included in a Mayor''s EO)                       |\n| 2       | Indicators owned      | Part C indicator codes and statements from IAT v1.7                                                                |\n| 3       | Focal persons         | Positions and alternates on both sides                                                                             |\n| 4       | Actions for the year  | From the IAT recommended actions and the CAPA register; outputs and dates                                          |\n| 5       | Information exchanged | What the CDRRMO supplies (hazard maps, scenarios, event data) and what the lead office supplies (evidence, status) |\n| 6       | Role in events        | PDRA participation; anticipatory actions; reporting to the EOC                                                     |\n| 7       | Review                | Annual interface review; self-scoring with validation by another office                                            |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch8v1_Annex_8-C.md (Chapter 8, v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7))','draft'),
('afeb01a9-2658-5b55-8570-8d1658efd57d'::uuid,'c01c2a2c-ad39-5d76-8c53-cd7de830f341'::uuid,'v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7)',E'# Annex 8-D. Agenda of the Annual Partner Forum\n\n**Table 8.36**\n\n*Annual Partner Forum Agenda*\n\n| **No.** | **Item**                         | **Output**                                                                      |\n|---------|----------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| 1       | Season outlook and hazard update | Shared understanding of the coming season (PAGASA products presented as issued) |\n| 2       | What we learned last season      | AAR findings involving partners; agreed improvements                            |\n| 3       | Partner register review          | Confirmed roles, contacts and commitments; lapsing agreements identified        |\n| 4       | Interfaces and lifelines         | Status of Part C actions and utility arrangements                               |\n| 5       | Inclusion and accountability     | Input from sectoral, faith-based and community groups                           |\n| 6       | Exercises for the year           | Partner participation in the exercise calendar (Chapter 9)                      |\n| 7       | Actions                          | Owners and dates entered in the CAPA register                                   |\n\n# Validation and Source Control Register\n\n**Table 8.37**\n\n*Validation and Source Control Register*\n\n| **Item**                              | **Source used**                                                                                         | **Status**                                                     |\n|---------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------|\n| IAT rows and scores                   | IAT v1.7 workbook in the repository (12 Nov 2026)                                                       | Pending validation, 1–4 December 2026                          |\n| Inter-LGU assistance records          | CDRRMC and SP resolutions in the City issuances register                                                | Attach copies in the Vault                                     |\n| CPR-RIMT MOA                          | SP Res. No. 2023-347; annexed copy unsigned                                                             | Obtain and file the signed copy                                |\n| CCCM Team EO number                   | Register: filed as No. 263; scan reads 243                                                              | Confirm with the City Secretary                                |\n| Cluster citation                      | IAT cites NDCC MC No. 12, s. 2008; DILG VIII SOP cites NDCC Circular No. 5, s. 2007 and No. 04, s. 2008 | Confirm with OCD VIII                                          |\n| RA 10121 Sec. 12(c) item for linkages | Cited in IAT v1.7 as item (15)                                                                          | Check against the official text                                |\n| CSO accreditation status              | Not shown in the document set                                                                           | SP Secretariat to confirm                                      |\n| Faith-based partners                  | None found                                                                                              | Invite to the first partner forum                              |\n| Augmentation route and regional SOPs  | National Disaster Response Plan; RDRRMC VIII practice                                                   | Confirm the current request route with the PDRRMO and OCD VIII |\n','Loaded from reference/moo/MOO_Ch8v1_Annex_8-D.md (Chapter 8, v1.0 working draft (IAT v1.7))','draft'),
('72c76001-de05-5658-b23b-27171551e508'::uuid,'d47f0498-4189-5772-9e6c-fecd708e1cbc'::uuid,'v0.1 proposed (EOC Module note, 6 Nov 2026)',E'# SOP 6-GIS-01 | Establishment, Updating and Operational Use of the EOC Geospatial Common Operating Picture\n\n**Status:** proposed SOP for the EOC Operations, Information Management, Logistics and Coordination chapter (MOO Chapter 6, not yet drafted). Loaded as a controlled draft so the Geo-COP workflow (WF-GEO-COP) points to an existing text. Source: the 6 November 2026 note "Proposed Enhancement to the EOC Module: Geospatial Operations and Common Operating Picture", section 3, unchanged except for this header.\n\nTitle: Establishment, Updating and Operational Use of the EOC Geospatial Common Operating Picture\n\nPurpose: To ensure that the EOC maintains a consistent, validated and operationally useful geographic representation of incidents, affected areas, facilities, resources and response operations.\n\n| Step                          | Responsible actor                                      | Required action                                                                                                                 | Output / control                          |\n| ----------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------- |\n| 1. Establish reference        | EOC Information Management function / CDRRMO           | Register the EOC point from the supplied KML and verify the coordinates through field validation.                               | EOC geospatial reference register         |\n| 2. Acquire datasets           | EOC Information Management function                    | Obtain available base maps, hazard layers, administrative boundaries and critical-facility datasets from authorized custodians. | Geospatial data inventory                 |\n| 3. Validate data              | Designated data custodian / technical office           | Check source, date, coordinate system, geometry, completeness and consistency.                                                  | Data validation record                    |\n| 4. Integrate layers           | EOC Information Management function                    | Load approved datasets into the designated GIS or mapping platform and apply agreed layer naming and symbology.                 | Geo-COP operational map                   |\n| 5. Plot incident information  | EOC Situation Unit or designated information personnel | Record incident locations and spatially reference reports received from barangays, field teams and agencies.                    | Georeferenced incident records            |\n| 6. Verify field information   | Concerned technical office / field team                | Confirm material incident locations, access constraints and reported impacts through appropriate field verification.            | Verification status and supporting report |\n| 7. Update operational picture | EOC Information Management function                    | Update incident, evacuation, resource and infrastructure layers as validated information becomes available.                     | Time-stamped Geo-COP                      |\n| 8. Disseminate                | EOC Manager / authorized information officer           | Share approved map products with decision-makers and operational partners according to access permissions.                      | Situation map / map briefing              |\n| 9. Archive and review         | EOC Information Management function                    | Preserve operational map versions and underlying records for incident review, reporting and after-action analysis.              | Archived map versions and metadata        |\n\nOperational control: Each map product shall indicate its preparation date and time, data sources, verification status and intended use. Preliminary or unverified information must be visibly distinguished from confirmed information.\n\nThe SOP should be activated as part of the EOC''s information-management function whenever the EOC is activated. During normal operations, the CDRRMO shall maintain the underlying datasets, registers and readiness arrangements.\n\n**Related records in MODE:** forms EOC-GIS-REF and EOC-GIS-01 to EOC-GIS-04; EOC → Map (ADR-015). Chapter 4 (SOP 4-05) uses the Geo-COP for the incident situation; Chapter 6 owns this procedure when drafted.\n','Loaded from reference/moo/SOP_6-GIS-01_proposed.md (Area 6, v0.1 proposed (EOC Module note, 6 Nov 2026))','draft')
